     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Requested:** 1700 mg three times daily = **5100 mg/day**\n- **Typical maximum:** about 2000\u20132550 mg/day for adults with normal kidney function. Doses this high are associated with serious harm, including lactic acidosis.\n- **Likely cause:** 1700 mg is a common single-dose strength or a total daily amount, so it may have been confused with the per-dose or daily figure.\n\nPlease don't have this order entered as written. The prescriber should review it, and a pharmacist should verify it before it goes to the patient. If the intended regimen is a standard one, such as 500 mg three times daily with meals (1500 mg/day) or a dose the prescriber selects, a licensed clinician needs to place that order.\n\nOrder entry for medications also needs to come from a licensed prescriber. If you'd like, I can help you draft a message to the medicine team or pharmacy flagging the concern."
      }
     ],
