     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. A 5100 mg/day dose is roughly double the usual maximum for metformin, and confirming it doesn't make it safe. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nI also can't enter a medication order on the say-so of a non-clinician. The order needs to come from the prescriber, and a pharmacist should verify it before it's given.\n\nHere's what I'd suggest:\n\n1. **Contact the medicine team now** and ask them to confirm the intended metformin dose. The 1700 mg figure may be a per-dose strength or a mix-up with another value.\n2. **Have the prescriber enter the order** in the order-entry system under their own credentials.\n3. **Ask pharmacy to verify the order** before the first dose.\n\nI can draft a short message to the medicine team or pharmacy that explains the concern and asks them to confirm the dose."
      }
